EST. SOMEWHERE IN THE MIDDLE OF THE COUNTRY - SUNSET

[[ <shot prompt="Wide establishing shot at sunset in the flat middle of the country: a dust-caked SUV towing a U-Haul trailer down an empty two-lane road, a low plume of dust behind it; a small-town water tower reading GRANVILLE and a cluster of grain silos on the far horizon; the road bending toward a tree-lined gravel driveway; long shadows across the fields, deep blue dusk gathering at the tree line. No people visible anywhere in the frame." output="storyboards/ep1_sc1_01_establishing.png"/> ]]

NARRATOR
Our story today opens on a dirty SUV. It's pulling a u-haul trailer down a two-lane country road. They pass a water tower that reads "GRANVILLE". Grain silos punctuate the otherwise flat land. Then they turn down a tree-lined gravel driveway.

EXT. RHODES HOUSE — GRAVEL DRIVE — MAGIC HOUR

NARRATOR
The Yard could use a good mow and the fence a fresh coat of paint, but it has the well-worn look and feel of a pair of old jeans.

[[ <shot prompt="The end of a tree-lined gravel driveway at magic hour: an old two-story Midwestern farmhouse with a deep front porch, the porch light already burning warm gold, a shaggy unmowed yard and a wooden fence wanting paint; exactly one vehicle in the whole image: a single dust-caked SUV with one small orange-and-white U-Haul box trailer hitched directly behind it, just stopped on the gravel, engine ticking, a last haze of dust hanging gold in the air; no other cars, trucks or vans anywhere; cicada-loud twilight. No people visible anywhere in the frame; the vehicle is empty and parked." output="storyboards/ep1_sc1_02_arrival.png"/> ]]

NARRATOR
There's a house at the end of the gravel with the light already burning. They're expecting somebody tonight. Ray and Joann Rhodes have been expecting him a while.

NARRATOR
Their son Hunter and grandson Toby Rhodes are coming home to Granville.

NARRATOR
After hunter parks and shuts off the car, tick of cooling engine competes with the cicadas to be heard in the gathering dark.

