[[ <shot prompt="Medium shot on the porch at night: the slim dark-haired man of thirty-nine stopped mid-pace, mouth open, all the fight gone out of him; a man in his late forties with thick jet-black hair and a dense black beard, in a plain grey work shirt, seated and looking down at his hands as he speaks; behind them a much heavier man of thirty-nine with short untidy sandy light-brown hair, in a red plaid shirt, wearing an exaggerated worried face; warm porch bulb, deep blue night beyond the rail. The slim dark-haired man is the man from the first reference image, in a maroon sweater. The black-haired, black-bearded man is the man from the second reference image, fully clothed in a plain grey rolled-sleeve work shirt and jeans, no plaid. The heavy sandy-haired man is the man from the third reference image, in a red plaid shirt. Exactly three people in the image. Each person has exactly two arms and two hands; each hand has five fingers with natural proportions. No extra fingers, no extra hands, no extra arms. No text or lettering anywhere in the image." ref="KEVIN,HUNTER,GARETH" output="storyboards/ep1_sc1_11_the-hidden-burden.png"/> ]]

This takes the wind out of Kevin’s sails. Gareth pulls a super-concerned face.

KEVIN
Whaaaat?

HUNTER
Toby called me and told me the janitor had to drive him home and Mom won’t come out of the bathroom. When I got there, Toby hadn’t eaten since the day before.

GARETH
Hunter, We had no idea.

HUNTER
She wouldn’t let me tell anyone. She was scared it would get back to her friends. The important part is that Toby is here. He’s happy, healthy and being spoiled rotten by his grandparents. I’m here now Kevin. Will you let me help where I can?

KEVIN
Be careful what you ask for.

